async def wallet_payment_send(
    client: Client,
    request: WalletPaymentSendRequest,
) -> WalletPaymentSendResponse:
    """Enqueue a payment from a wallet: `POST /v1/wallets/{id}/transactions`.

    Enqueues one send job of `asset` from the keyed wallet: one payment, signed as one transaction and broadcast. Several payments are several requests; a wallet's sends run one at a time, in order, and each fails on its own. A 202 response means queued, not submitted: `GET /v1/jobs/{id}` reports the outcome. Indexing records the transaction once it is mined, for the assets the wallet is watched in. A watch-only wallet answers 422, as does a wallet whose index of `asset` (and, for a token, of `native`, which pays the fee) is missing: there is no balance to check. A paused index still sends, and its transaction is recorded once mined.
    """
    return SendAccepted.from_json(await client.send(request))


